\frametitle{Macros}
\center
\bl{Macros} provide a mechanism for defining reusable, named constructs that encapsulate both \bl{content} and \bl{formatting}.
\tiny
\begin{verbatim}
	\newcommand{\quartet}{\href{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anscombe\%27s_quartet}{Anscombe's data set quartet}}
\end{verbatim}
\normalsize
		\begin{itemize}
			\item The macro \verb|\quartet| defines a single semantic reference that consistently expands to a hyperlink to \quartet
		\end{itemize}
